  "body": "## What is missing\n\nCamCraft has no laser cut operation. A search of `crates/app/src` on `origin/main` finds no laser operation type. Plasma has `PlasmaProfile` (#1870 gives it DXF sketch chains). Wire EDM has the Wire Contour on DXF chains (#2022).\n\nThe maintainer asked for laser cuts on placed DXF sketches in chat on 2026-11-15 (quoted in #2022):\n\n> A DXF should be possible to \"place\" on a stock and used as references for cutting - not be treated like a model - thus for processes like wireedm, plasma, laser, etc etc.. we can just make a sheet, cube, cylinder. place the DXF - and select operations accordingly.\n\n#2022 item 3 said: if no laser operation exists, file the issue for it. This is that issue.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. A laser profile operation on DXF sketch chains, with per-chain side and direction, as for the plasma profile (#1870).\n2. The kerf offset (beam kerf) uses the same offset and verify laws as the plasma profile. An offset that cannot fit refuses by name.\n3. Pierce and lead data: reuse the plasma pierce model where it applies (#1521).\n4. A post dialect for at least one laser control, or a statement that the generic post covers it.\n5. The commands have their MCP tools, or a follow-up issue `MCP: <command>`.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A laser profile cut on a placed DXF sketch generates, verifies and posts.\n- Tests pin the kerf side, a refusal by name, and the posted output.\n\nRefs #2022, #1870, #1521.\n",
